  {
   "t": "li",
   "x": "“When universities propose to transform their curricula by integrating artificial intelligence” 变成 When引导时间状语从句；by integrating为“介词+动名词” 变成 用于交代背景或条件，并用by doing说明方式。"
  },
  {
   "t": "li",
   "x": "“arguing that commercial pressure could undermine the educational values that have long shaped academic life” 变成 现在分词短语作伴随状语；that引导宾语从句，第二个that引导定语从句 变成 用分词补充说明批评者的观点，并用嵌套从句增强信息密度。"
  },
  {
   "t": "li",
   "x": "“They resist the assumption that every innovation necessarily improves learning” 变成 resist后接名词宾语；that引导同位语从句 变成 用that解释assumption的具体内容，resist常表示“抵制某种观念、做法”。"
  },
  {
   "t": "li",
   "x": "“A wiser approach is not to reject change altogether but to examine who benefits from it and who bears its costs” 变成 not...but...连接两个不定式；两个who引导并列宾语从句 变成 用not...but...构成对比，用who从句分别说明受益者与承担者。"
  },
  {
   "t": "li",
   "x": "“Only when institutions support careful trial and open discussion can reform truly serve education rather than merely serve the market” 变成 Only+when状语从句置句首引起主句部分倒装；rather than连接并列动词短语 变成 用倒装强调“只有……才……”，用rather than表达取舍与对比。"
  }
 ]
}
